  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-11-05T03:57:51.457Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I don't know if this is a specific bug with Poiyomi or Material contacts in general but i after testing with a few friends we noticed that material contacts when  they come in contact with someones contacts that have a armature that is improperly scaled to 100 100 100 instead of 1 1 1 sets off the material contact to Max instead of reacting to where they touch.\n\nI did a simple disolve material contact and most people can just touch part of my avatar and it will disolve where their index finger contacts are but then when people index finger contact touch the material contact it sets it to max and makes my whole avatar disappear.  We narrowed it down after testing many different avatars that it only happened with avatars that have the 100 100 100 scale on their avatar's armature in unity.",
